## --out writes the same documents to a file
$ go run ./cmd/seed --machines 5 --trials 100 --seed 42 --out seed.json
seed: 5 machines x 225 configurations x 100 trials = 112500 measurement rows
seed: generated 112500 rows in 30 runs in 28ms
seed: wrote /tmp/claude-1000/-home-matthewlee-benchmark-platform/f5e09172-3231-40fc-b29f-1efd9bcd51fd/scratchpad/seed.json (43.0 MB)

## The floor is enforced: a small run refuses to exit 0
$ go run ./cmd/seed --machines 1 --trials 10 --out /dev/null ; echo "exit=$?"
seed: 1 machines x 225 configurations x 10 trials = 2250 measurement rows
seed: generated 2250 rows in 6 runs in 1ms
seed: wrote /dev/null (0.0 MB)
seed: 2250 rows is below the 100000-row floor; pass --allow-small if that is intended
exit status 1
exit=1

$ go run ./cmd/seed --machines 1 --trials 10 --allow-small --out /dev/null ; echo "exit=$?"
seed: 1 machines x 225 configurations x 10 trials = 2250 measurement rows
seed: generated 2250 rows in 6 runs in 1ms
seed: wrote /dev/null (0.0 MB)
exit=0

## Determinism, at the level of the file
$ go run ./cmd/seed --seed 42 --out a.json && go run ./cmd/seed --seed 42 --out b.json && cmp a.json b.json
identical (cmp exit 0)
$ go run ./cmd/seed --seed 43 --out c.json && cmp a.json c.json
/tmp/claude-1000/-home-matthewlee-benchmark-platform/f5e09172-3231-40fc-b29f-1efd9bcd51fd/scratchpad/a.json /tmp/claude-1000/-home-matthewlee-benchmark-platform/f5e09172-3231-40fc-b29f-1efd9bcd51fd/scratchpad/c.json differ: byte 33, line 2
